Subject: Extend the in-place string accumulator to chained concatenation

What this does
  Extend the in-place string accumulator to chained concatenation.

Why we need it
  A `'a' + x + 'b'` chain allocated two strings where the stack VM allocates one: the accumulator only fired when destination == left operand, the constant right operand of a chain reached the interpreter through `binary_cpool`'s non-pool branch which had no accumulator call, and no scatter hint gave the intermediate headroom to extend into.

What it adds
  Sets `js_scat_hint` in `js_regvm_binary`'s ADD path and gives the non-pool constant branches of threaded `regvm_t_binary_cpool` and monolith `L_ROP_binary_cpool` the same `regvm_accum_append` call the pool branch has; step helpers regenerated.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
